description:
Replaces wyrd-v2gm.18. Define register_effects.yaml catalog and composition semantics.

CATALOG SCHEMA:
Each register effect = triple of (phonological_feature_weights, semantic_tag_weights, position_bias). E.g.:

  harsh:
    phonological: {cluster_density: +0.6, final_fortition: +0.5, vowel_final_bias: -0.4}
    semantic_tags: {}
    position_bias: {}

  grim:
    phonological: {}
    semantic_tags: {death: +0.7, monster: +0.5, undead: +0.6, magic: +0.4, military: +0.3}
    position_bias: {}

  pastoral:
    phonological: {vowel_final_bias: +0.2, soft_consonants: +0.3}
    semantic_tags: {plant: +0.5, water: +0.5, agriculture: +0.6, tree: +0.4, bird: +0.4}

INITIAL ENTRIES (migration from MOODS): grim, harsh, pastoral, devotional, mortuary. Plus new entries the design discussion surfaced: noble, mystical, melodic, sinister, ancient, exotic, martial.

COMPOSITION RULES:
- Multiple effects sum component-wise (phonological vectors add, semantic tag weights add, position biases add)
- Clamp final composed vector to [-1, 1] per dimension
- Colon-suffix graduation (e.g. 'harsh:0.5') multiplies the effect's contribution by 0.5
- Order-independent (sum is commutative)

OPERATOR PATH FOR CUSTOM EFFECTS: edit register_effects.yaml; no code changes required.

ACCEPTANCE: catalog YAML round-trips through Python dataclass; existing 5 moods' compositions produce vectors that, when applied to corpus etymons via Phase A vectors, select the same name distributions the old MOODS dict produced (within seed-stable tolerance).

